# Commit bodies carrying a line that reads as a `Bench:` footer without being one.
#
# EMPTY, and it stays that way. The one entry this file was created for is gone:
# the commit that broke every architecture lane quoted a gate result as
#
#     bench                                                2829394
#
# which upstream's pre-push hook regex matches -- `[ :]\+` spans the run of
# spaces -- so a reader scanning bodies line by line took it for the anchor. The
# value was true when written and went stale at the rebase onto 5062aee5, whose
# own history carries `Bench: 2884956`.
#
# It was baselined rather than reworded because rewording moves every SHA after
# it, and this file said to reword if the history was ever rewritten for another
# reason. It then was, to move the ipa-icf flag ahead of the seam thunk it
# guards, so the line became `bench nodes ... 2829394` in the same rewrite. What
# follows `bench` has to be spaces or colons and then a digit, and `nodes` is
# neither, so the loose form no longer matches it.
#
# A new entry means a commit message that a lane can misread. Reword it instead:
# an unpushed commit costs nothing to reword, and a pushed one costs what this
# file already spent.
